}
```

It checks `BadPart` first and then just calls the real `capture` and `release`. That way the fee rules, refusals and audit events are exactly theirs, in that order, and nothing is released when `part === amount`. If `release` refuses after `capture` has already run, `atomic()` puts back the balances and audit events.

